      },
      "lineNbr": 589,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000294
      },
      "writtenOn": "2012-10-10T16:08:37Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "So this is different from keys_changed in that it looks at debounced_state., whereas keys_changes looks at the raw state. Is that what you intend? It\u0027s arguable which one we want I think. But it seems a bit inconsistent to use both, since we use key_changed to break out of this loop, and num_keys_pressed to decide whether to go back to interrupt mode.\n\nWhat if the debounce supresses a key release then we break out, re-enable interrupts and now will never see that release and will be stuck in interrupt?",
      "revId": "e1ec457ad1fd64d64972f43840846ad0e6b1c8bf",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "AAAAQX///n0\u003d",
        "filename": "chip/stm32/keyboard_scan.c",
        "patchSetId": 6
      },
      "lineNbr": 589,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000253
      },
      "writtenOn": "2012-10-10T19:17:40Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Both look at the debounced state in this patch. I think the confusion here stems from changing the return value of check_keys_changed(). In this patch, the return value indicates whether or not the debounced state has changed.\n\nSo there are really two distinct values at work here -- the number of keys which have changed since the last scan (if \u003e0 we\u0027ll interrupt the host), and the total number of keys pressed (if \u003e0 we\u0027ll do another scan).\n\nIf a key release has yet to be detected, num_keys_pressed will be \u003e0 and we\u0027ll always do another scan, even if a previous change (ie keypress) caused the loop to break to notify the host. Then when the key release shows up in the debounced state, check_keys_changed() returns 1 and num_keys_pressed will be set to 0. So we\u0027ll break out, interrupt the host, and re-enable keyboard interrupts.",
      "parentUuid": "AAAAQX///6U\u003d",
      "revId": "e1ec457ad1fd64d64972f43840846ad0e6b1c8bf",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": false
    },
